# Untracked files copied into each new worktree (gitignore syntax: one pattern
# per line, # for comments, ! to negate an earlier pattern).
#
# Read by BB IDE and by the worktree-create skill. Both copy every UNTRACKED
# file in the source checkout that matches a pattern, BEFORE .bb-env-setup.sh
# runs — which is what lets that script rewrite the copies for the worktree.
#
# Rules (enforced by the copier, not by this file):
#   * files only — symlinks in the source checkout are skipped
#   * nothing already in the worktree is replaced (tracked files win)
#   * a pattern that matches nothing is reported, not fatal
#
# This file must be COMMITTED: a worktree only checks out tracked files.

# @@SECTION:ENV@@
# Local credentials and config the worktree needs. Copied, not shared —
# .env-setup.sh rewrites the path/port variables in these copies so a worktree
# can never write to the main checkout's real sinks.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# @@SECTION:EXTRA@@
# Other untracked, SMALL files the project needs at runtime or in tests
# (local certs, harness allowlists, scratch dirs). One line each, with why.
# .claude/settings.local.json

# @@SECTION:EXCLUDED@@
# NOT copied on purpose — keep this list; it stops the next person "fixing" it:
#   node_modules/ .venv/ target/   — rebuilt by the setup script; BB copies
#                                    directories file by file, which is slow
#                                    and leaves broken absolute shebangs
#   *.db / *.sqlite                — a plain copy of a live (WAL) database can
#                                    be torn; the setup script snapshots it
